                    <msContents>
                        <summary>Averroës' Middle Commentary on Aristotle's <title>Analytica
                                Priora</title> and <title>Analytica Posteriora</title>. </summary>
                        <msItem>
                            <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="">Kitāb al-Talkhīṣ</title>
                            <title xml:lang="ar" type="alt">كتاب التلخيص</title>
                            <title xml:lang="en" type="alt">Middle Commentary</title>
                            <author key="person_19688718"><persName xml:lang="en">Averroës,
                                    1126-1198</persName> (<persName xml:lang="ar">ابن رشد، محمد بن
                                    احمد</persName>)</author>
                            <note><p>The commentator is not mentioned by name. Mingana (1934)
                                    presumed that he was Muḥammad bin Muḥammad al-Fārābī. This title
                                    is found at the end of both treatises in the present manuscript.
                                    Erwin I.J. Rosenthal (1937) identified the author as Averroës,
                                    see his article in the BJRL 21, no.2.</p></note>


                            <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14049_item_1-item_1">
                                <locus from="2a" to="36a">2a-36a</locus>
                                <title xml:lang="en">Commentary on the Analytica Priora</title>
                                <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                                <note><p>The Analytica Priora of Aristotle in Arabic is entitled:
                                        Kitāb al-Qiyās (<quote xml:lang="ar">كتاب القياس</quote>);
                                        Book of Syllogism).</p>
                                    <p>The manuscript is imperfect at the beginning. From the lack
                                        of the first page (or pages) there is nothing to supply a
                                        proper description of the manuscript and the text begins
                                        abruptly.</p>
                                    <p>Quotations from Aristotle are introduced by
                                            <quote>قال</quote>, but there is no <quote>اقول</quote>
                                        preceding the commentary.</p>
                                    <p>This book of al-Qiyās is referred to in the following
                                        treatise where we read on folio 48a: <quote>لانه ليس يلزم عن
                                            وجود التالي وجود المقدم على ما تبين في كتاب
                                            القياس</quote>.</p></note>
                                <incipit>البيان بالدور كما قلنا فى الصنف الاول من الشكل
                                    الاول</incipit>
                            </msItem>

                            <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14049_item_1-item_2">
                                <locus from="36a" to="95a">36a-95a</locus>
                                <title xml:lang="en">Commentary on the Analytica Posteriora</title>

                                <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                                <note><p> Aristotle's work is entitled in Arabic: Kitāb al-Burhān
                                            (<quote xml:lang="ar">كتاب البرهان</quote>); Book of
                                        Argumentation).</p>
                                    <p>It is divided into two maqālahs, each preceded with a
                                        Basmallah.</p>
                                </note>
                                <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14049_item_1-item_2-item_1">
                                    <locus from="36a" to="79a">36a-79a</locus>
                                    <title>Maqālah 1</title>
                                    <incipit>قال كل تعليم وكل تعلم فكرى فانما يكون بمعرفة متقذمة
                                        للمتعلم</incipit>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14049_item_1-item_2-item_2">
                                    <locus from="79a" to="95a">79a-95a</locus>
                                    <title>Maqālah 2</title>
                                    <note><p>It is entitled: <quote xml:lang="ar">المقالة الثانية من
                                                تلخيص كتاب البرهان لاريطو</quote>.</p></note>
                                </msItem>
                            </msItem>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
