                        <sealDesc>
                            <summary>Three types of rectangular vermilion library seal impressions,
                                intaglio-carved in nastaʿlīq script in two stacked lines, of the
                                kings of <placeName ref="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/tgn/7001502"
                                    key="place_7001502">Awadh (Oude)</placeName> appear on <locus
                                    from="1a">folio 1a</locus> and <locus from="95b"
                                >95b</locus>.</summary>
                            <seal type="stamp" subtype="rectangle">
                                <p> Library seal of <persName role="fmo seal"
                                        ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/265857376" key="person_265857376"
                                        >Nāṣir al-Dīn Ḥaydar Shāh (b. 1803, r. 1827–1837)</persName>
                                    dated <date calendar="#Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1828"
                                        notAfter="1829"> 1244 AH (1828–29 CE)</date>, inscribed with
                                    his title <addName type="epithet"
                                        ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/265857376" key="person_265857376"
                                        >Sulaymān Jāh</addName> within two stacked, single-ruled
                                    cartouches:</p>
                                <decoNote type="stamp" subtype="inscription"><p><quote xml:lang="fa"
                                            > خوش است مهر کتبخانه سلیمان جاه * بهر کتاب مزین چو نقش
                                            بسم الله، ١٢۴۴</quote></p>
                                    <p>
                                        <quote xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Khvush ast muhur-i
                                                kitābkhānah-'i Sulaymān Jāh bahr-i kitāb; muzayyin
                                                chaw naqsh-i basmallah</hi>, <date
                                                calendar="#Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1828-07-14"
                                                notAfter="1829-07-02">1244 </date></quote> (<quote
                                            xml:lang="en">The seal of the library of Sulaymān Jāh is
                                            good; it embellishes the book like the design of a <hi
                                                rend="italic">basmallah</hi>, <date
                                                calendar="#Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1828-07-14"
                                                notAfter="1829-07-02">1244</date></quote>).</p>
                                    <p><dimensions type="seal" unit="mm">
                                            <height>17</height>
                                            <width>37</width>
                                        </dimensions></p></decoNote>
                            </seal>
                            <seal>
                                <p>Library seal, surmounted by the royal emblem of Awadh, of
                                        <persName role="fmo seal"
                                        key="person_9680150325559110090006"
                                        ref="https://viaf.org/viaf/9680150325559110090006/">Amjad
                                        ‘Alī Shāh (b. 1801, r. 1842–1847)</persName>, dotted-ruled
                                    and dated <date calendar="#Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1844-01-22"
                                        notAfter="1845-01-09">1260 AH (1844–45 CE):</date></p>
                                <decoNote type="stamp" subtype="inscription"><p><quote xml:lang="fa"
                                            >ناسخ هر مهر شد چون شد مزین بر کتاب * خاتم امجد علی شاه
                                            زمان عالیجناب، ١٢٦٠</quote></p>
                                    <p><quote xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc"><hi rend="italic">Nāsukh har
                                                muhur shud chun shud muzayyin bar kitāb; khātim-i
                                                Amjad ‘Alī Shāh zamān-i ‘Ālījanāb</hi>, <date
                                                calendar="#Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1844-01-22"
                                                notAfter="1845-01-09">1260</date></quote> (<quote
                                            xml:lang="en">Every [prior] seal became cancelled since
                                            the book became embellished by the seal of Amjad ‘Alī
                                            Shāh in the era of his Sublime Majesty, <date
                                                calendar="#Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1844-01-22"
                                                notAfter="1845-01-09">1260</date></quote>).</p>
                                    <p><dimensions type="seal" unit="mm">
                                            <height>53</height>
                                            <width>45</width>
                                        </dimensions></p></decoNote>
                            </seal>
                            <seal>
                                <p>Library seal, surmounted by the royal emblem Awadh, of <persName
                                        ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/305855167" role="fmo seal"
                                        key="person_305855167">Wājid ‘Alī Shāh (b. 1822, r.
                                        1847–1856)</persName>, single-ruled and dated <date
                                        calendar="#Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1846" notAfter="1847"
                                        >1262 AH (1846–47 CE)</date>:</p>
                                <decoNote type="stamp" subtype="inscription"><p><quote xml:lang="fa"
                                            > خاتم واجد علی سلطان عالم بر کتاب * ثابت و پر نور بادا
                                            تا فروغ آفتاب، ١٢۶۲ </quote></p>
                                    <p><quote xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc"><hi rend="italic">Khātim-i
                                                Wājid ‘Alī, Sulṭān-i ‘Ālam bar kitāb, s̄abit va pur
                                                nūr bādā tā farūgh-i āftāb</hi>, 1262</quote>
                                            (<quote xml:lang="en">The seal of Wājid ‘Alī, Sulṭān of
                                            the World, upon the book shall be permanent and as
                                            bright as sunlight, <date calendar="#Hijri-qamari"
                                                notBefore="1844-01-22" notAfter="1845-01-09">1262 AH
                                                [1847 CE]</date></quote>).</p>
                                    <p><dimensions type="seal" unit="mm">
                                            <height>41</height>
                                            <width>26</width>
                                        </dimensions></p></decoNote>
                            </seal>

                        </sealDesc>
